{
  "id": "argonia-groundcover-v2",
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "status": "ACTIVE \u2014 the land-cover base is the mined Bethesda GRAS binding; the region layer above it is decision 0048. Schema is Bethesda's GRAS field list, adopted as a checklist per module 95 \u00a786.0b.",
  "grounding": {
    "schema": "docs/research/placement-settlements/shipped-world-placement-rules.md R10: GRAS carries density, slope limits, a distance-from-water rule with a mode enum, position jitter, height/colour variance and a wind wave period; LTEX.GNAM binds grasses to painted ground and never allows more than three",
    "observedValues": "world/sources/placement/groundcover-rules.json",
    "landCoverIds": "tooling/world-generation/worldgen/landcover.py \u2014 the same ids the ground-control raster stores in its red channel",
    "regionClasses": "tooling/world-generation/worldgen/regions.py \u2014 the same ids apps/world-studio/public/province/hydro-regions.png stores by colour",
    "why": "v1 was keyed by land cover ALONE, so the tidal delta, the interior swamp and the mangrove coast got identical grass wherever they shared a cover id. `vurt_reeds` carried MARSH_GRASS, SWAMP_GRASS and SCUM, so every reed bed in Black Marsh was the same plant. Region grammar drives everything (00-core rule 7). Round 13 took the ring kit from 7 meshes to 34 and spread them. No mesh now carries more than two land covers. The thinnest region holds three species where it held one."
  },
  "rules": {
    "maxSpeciesPerCover": 3,
    "maxCoversPerSpeciesPerRegion": 2,
    "resolution": "species for (region class, land cover) = byRegionClass[region].swaps[cover] when present, else byLandCover[cover].species. A swap REPLACES the base list for that one cover in that one region; it never merges",
    "whyTheCapStillHolds": "LTEX.GNAM's limit of three is per painted TEXTURE, so it caps how many species may share one cover. It says nothing about the same cover carrying different species in different regions. The swap layer therefore fits inside the shipped-game rule rather than bending it",
    "bareGroundIsFine": "20 of the 47 mined landscape textures allow no grass at all; mud, silt, rock and road are meant to read bare",
    "tier": "T3 \u2014 regenerated at runtime from the land-cover raster inside a camera ring, never written into chunk bundles (module 65 \u00a7110)",
    "densityUnit": "instances per hectare inside the ring, before the slope response",
    "assetPool": "every asset here must be in tooling/asset-pipeline/pipeline/config/kits/groundcover-province-v1.json \u2014 the ring loads that one GLB. Adding a species is a kit rebuild, not a data edit. The kit carries 34 meshes (round 13); the triangle ceiling is 128, the shipped seven's own maximum."
  },
